`enable-favorites-bar` is false (embedded favorites bar), the condition would be false, and the favorites bar wouldn't show. But wait, if `enable-favorites-bar` is false, the embedded bar is used, and the embedded bar is always visible (it's embedded in the kiss bar). So hiding it wouldn't make sense. The current logic is correct.\n\nActually, re-reading: `isMinimalisticModeEnabledForFavorites()` returns:\n```java\nprefs.getBoolean(\"history-hide\", false) && prefs.getBoolean(\"favorites-hide\", false) && prefs.getBoolean(\"enable-favorites-bar\", true)\n```\n\nSo it requires `enable-favorites-bar` to be true. If `enable-favorites-bar` is false, this returns false, and the favorites bar is not shown on tap. But if `enable-favorites-bar` is false, the embedded favorites bar is used, which is always visible when the kiss bar is displayed. So this makes sense.\n\nOK, now I'm really going to implement the fix.\n\nHere's my plan:\n1. In the `doAction(\"display-history\")` case, move the `history-onclick` check inside, around the `HistorySearcher` block.\n2. In the gesture detector's tap handlers, remove the `history-onclick` check so `doAction(\"display-history\")` is always called.\n\nLet me write the code.\n","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0}}}
