{"type":"assistant","uuid":"0f55c0d6-8548-40e4-a1ca-a980122840c3","session_id":"b6db9417-93e9-42c0-ae53-1ecc09abc1e9","parent_tool_use_id":null,"message":{"id":"0f55c0d6-8548-40e4-a1ca-a980122840c3","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"qwen/qwen3.6-35b-a3b","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The QA suite confirms the expected behavior:\n\n> **Minimalistic mode on for favorites**\n> - Favorites bar is hidden by default\n> - **Touching the screen on an empty area displays history and the favorites**\n\nThe fix is clear. The bug is in `ExperienceTweaks.java`: the `history-onclick` setting gates the entire `doAction(\"display-history\")` call, which prevents the favorites bar from being shown when `history-onclick` is **disabled**. The favorites bar visibility should work independently of `history-onclick`.\n\n**Root cause:** In the gesture detector's `onSingleTapUp` and `onSingleTapConfirmed`, `doAction(\"display-history\")` is only called when `history-onclick` is enabled. This means the favorites bar (which is shown at the end of that case block) never appears when `history-onclick` is off.\n\n**Fix:** Move the `history-onclick` check inside the `doAction(\"display-history\")` case (around only the `HistorySearcher` block) and remove it from the tap handlers. This way the favorites bar shows unconditionally while the history search remains gated.\n\n"}],"stop_reason":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0}}}
