{"type":"assistant","uuid":"ce0e9b0a-f74d-4cfc-a251-1e160ebb2781","session_id":"b6db9417-93e9-42c0-ae53-1ecc09abc1e9","parent_tool_use_id":null,"message":{"id":"ce0e9b0a-f74d-4cfc-a251-1e160ebb2781","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"qwen/qwen3.6-35b-a3b","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The fix is verified and in place. Let me provide the complete summary and final patch.\n\n---\n\n## Bug Analysis & Fix Summary\n\n### Root Cause\n\nIn `ExperienceTweaks.java`, the gesture detector's tap handlers (`onSingleTapUp` and `onSingleTapConfirmed`) gated the `doAction(\"display-history\")` call behind the `history-onclick` preference:\n\n```java\n// BEFORE (buggy): history-onclick gates the entire method call\nif (prefs.getBoolean(\"history-onclick\", false)) {\n    doAction(\"display-history\");\n}\n```\n\nThe `doAction(\"display-history\")` method has two responsibilities:\n1. Run `HistorySearcher` (gated by `history-onclick` — correct)\n2. Show the favorites bar when minimalistic mode for favorites is enabled (NOT gated — **correct behavior**)\n\nSince `history-onclick` was the only gate for the entire method, the favorites bar never appeared on tap when `history-onclick` was disabled — even though showing the favorites bar should work independently.\n\n### Fix\n\nMoved the `history-onclick` check from the tap handlers **into** the `doAction(\"display-history\")` case, wrapping only the `HistorySearcher` block. This way:\n- The favorites bar shows on tap whenever `isMinimalisticModeEnabledForFavorites()` is true, regardless of `history-onclick`\n- The `HistorySearcher` still only runs when `history-onclick` is explicitly enabled\n\n### Final Patch\n\n```diff\n--- a/app/src/main/java/fr/neamar/kiss/forwarder/ExperienceTweaks.java\n+++ app/src/main/java/fr/neamar/kiss/forwarder/ExperienceTweaks.java\n@@ -75,9 +75,7 @@\n             public boolean onSingleTapUp(MotionEvent e) {\n                 // Double tap disabled: display history directly\n                 if(!prefs.getBoolean(\"double-tap\", false)) {\n-                    if (prefs.getBoolean(\"history-onclick\", false)) {\n-                        doAction(\"display-history\");\n-                    }\n+                    doAction(\"display-history\");\n                 }\n                 return super.onSingleTapUp(e);\n             }\n@@ -86,9 +84,7 @@\n             public boolean onSingleTapConfirmed(MotionEvent e) {\n                 // Double tap enabled: wait to confirm this is indeed a single tap, not a double tap\n                 if(prefs.getBoolean(\"double-tap\", false)) {\n-                    if (prefs.getBoolean(\"history-onclick\", false)) {\n-                        doAction(\"display-history\");\n-                    }\n+                    doAction(\"display-history\");\n                 }\n \n                 return super.onSingleTapConfirmed(e);\n@@ -155,15 +151,17 @@\n                         }\n                         break;\n                     case \"display-history\":\n-                        // if minimalistic mode is enabled,\n-                        if (isMinimalisticModeEnabled()) {\n-                            // and we're currently in minimalistic mode with no results,\n-                            // and we're not looking at the app list\n-                            if (mainActivity.isViewingSearchResults() && mainActivity.searchEditText.getText().toString().isEmpty()) {\n-                                if (mainActivity.list.getAdapter() == null || mainActivity.list.getAdapter().isEmpty()) {\n-                                    mainActivity.runTask(new HistorySearcher(mainActivity));\n-                                    mainActivity.clearButton.setVisibility(View.VISIBLE);\n-                                    mainActivity.menuButton.setVisibility(View.INVISIBLE);\n+                        // Run history search only if history-onclick is enabled\n+                        if (prefs.getBoolean(\"history-onclick\", false)) {\n+                            if (isMinimalisticModeEnabled()) {\n+                                // and we're currently in minimalistic mode with no results,\n+                                // and we're not looking at the app list\n+                                if (mainActivity.isViewingSearchResults() && mainActivity.searchEditText.getText().toString().isEmpty()) {\n+                                    if (mainActivity.list.getAdapter() == null || mainActivity.list.getAdapter().isEmpty()) {\n+                                        mainActivity.runTask(new HistorySearcher(mainActivity));\n+                                        mainActivity.clearButton.setVisibility(View.VISIBLE);\n+                                        mainActivity.menuButton.setVisibility(View.INVISIBLE);\n+                                    }\n                                 }\n                             }\n                         }\n```\n\n### Build Note\n\nThe project requires network access to resolve the Android Gradle Plugin 3.6.2 from `jcenter()` (now deprecated/unreachable). All network connections are blocked in this environment. When the patch is applied to a build-capable environment, the project should compile without code errors since only logic was moved around — no new types, methods, or imports were added."}],"stop_reason":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":84009,"output_tokens":1073,"cache_read_input_tokens":82368,"total_tokens":85082}}}
